      "content": "Given below are two statements :<br><br>Statement I : The identification of Ni<sup>2+</sup> is carried out by dimethyl glyoxime in the presence of NH<sub>4</sub>OH. <br><br>Statement II : The dimethyl glyoxime is a bidentate neutral ligand.<br><br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true."
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false."
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false."
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true."
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "D"
      ],
      "explanation": "<p><b>Statement I</b> is true. Dimethyl glyoxime (DMG) is a chelating reagent commonly used for the identification of Ni<sup>2+</sup> ions in aqueous solution. In the presence of ammonium hydroxide (NH<sub>4</sub>OH), Ni<sup>2+</sup> reacts with dimethyl glyoxime to form a deep red-colored complex, which can be used to confirm the presence of Ni<sup>2+</sup> ions.</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement II</b> is also true. Dimethyl glyoxime is a neutral bidentate ligand, which means it has two donor atoms that can coordinate with a metal ion, and its overall charge is neutral.</p>\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Salt Analysis Question 40 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.